<title>USA: U.S. March retail sales rev to up 0.1 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. March retail sales rev to up 0.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Commerce Department on Friday issued annual revisions of U.S. retail sales for the period January 1993 through March 1997.</p>
<p>Following are revisions to retail sales for March 1997 and February 1997, seasonally adjusted, in percent changes and billions of dollars. Percent changes also include year-ago comparisons.</p>
<p>Percent Changes:  Mar--(Prev)  Feb--(Prev) Mar97/96-(Prev)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	   0.1    0.2   1.5    1.5     5.8     5.7</p>
<p> Excluding Autos	0.5    0.5   0.7    0.9     6.1     6.0</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    -1.1   -0.6   3.9    3.3     5.0     4.9</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs: Mar-(Previous)    Feb-(Previous)</p>
<p> Retail Sales	 213.63   215.57    213.39   215.14</p>
<p> Excluding Autos    161.22   162.01    160.38   161.25</p>
<p> Auto Sales	    52.42    53.56     53.01    53.89</p>
<p> Durable Goods	 87.98    89.28     88.19    89.23</p>
<p> NonDurable Goods   125.65   126.29    125.20   125.91</p>
<p> Furniture Stores    11.64    11.93     11.63    11.90</p>
<p> Building Materials  11.96    11.86     11.79    11.67</p>
<p>    Billions of Dlrs:  Mar-(Previous)   Feb-(Previous)</p>
<p> Gen.Merch.Stores    27.71    27.49    27.58   27.41</p>
<p> Department Stores   21.82    21.64    21.66   21.50</p>
<p> Food Stores	   36.07    36.17    35.92   35.97</p>
<p> Grocery Stores	34.04    34.16    33.85   33.94</p>
<p> Gas Stations	  13.20    13.39    13.29   13.50</p>
<p> Apparel Stores	 9.81     9.73     9.71    9.67</p>
<p> Eat/Drink Places    20.31    20.47    20.31   20.49</p>
<p> Drug Stores	    8.11     8.02     8.05    7.95</p>
<p>The department initially reported U.S. retail sales data for March on April 11.</p>
